TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/cross-cutting/observability/alerting.md

Evidence:
  - Google SRE Book
  - Alerting Best Practices
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [A1] Alert on symptoms, not causes.
  [A2] Every alert MUST have a runbook.
  [A3] Use severity levels (critical, warning, info).
  [A4] Implement on-call rotation.
  [A5] Use escalation policies.
  [A6] Alert on SLO violations, not just thresholds.
  [A7] Review and tune alerts regularly.
  [A8] Use silence/blackout windows for maintenance.

Pros:
  - Fast incident response
  - Proactive monitoring
  - User impact reduction

Cons:
  - Alert fatigue
  - On-call burden
  - False positives

Alternatives:
  - Manual monitoring
  - ChatOps
  - Self-healing systems

State: +

